diff --git a/docs/testing.md b/docs/testing.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f04e8f0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/testing.md
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+# Testing EFCC System
+
+Use the pinned Node 24.21.0 and pnpm 10.33.2. Bootstrap once with `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` and `pnpm exec playwright install chromium webkit`. Commit hooks never download dependencies or browsers.
+
+## Commands
+
+| Command | Boundary |
+| --- | --- |
+| `pnpm test` | Fast Node Vitest: pure contracts, SSR markup and test-gate checks |
+| `pnpm typecheck` | Compile contracts and generated Worker runtime types |
+| `pnpm test:e2e` | Complete local HTTP/Worker/D1 and browser inventory |
+| `pnpm test:e2e account-identity.spec.ts` | One affected feature with required configured projects |
+| `pnpm test:e2e --project=http` | HTTP-only claims, once each |
+| `pnpm test:resilience` | Tagged real fault/deadline/race cases |
+| `pnpm test:e2e --list` | Read-only discovery, without migrations/server/vars |
+| `pnpm test:presentation` | Existing journeys and responsive checks with masked images enabled |
+| `pnpm test:precommit` | Validate the staged tree, with conservative risk selection |
+
+`http` uses request contexts, native auth and real D1; it is not a mocked unit suite. Chromium and the existing iPhone WebKit/Pixel Chromium review profiles retain browser claims. Tags classify individual claims within mixed files; resilience is a concern across HTTP and browser tests, not a separate fake runtime. Existing browser journeys continue to assert durable effects where needed.
+
+## State and fixture ownership
+
+The runner exports tracked and non-ignored working files into an owned temporary directory. Staged checks export the Git index instead, so an unstaged fix cannot conceal a staged bug. Ignored developer `.dev.vars`, `.wrangler`, build output and session artifacts are never copied. Each invocation owns synthetic secrets, D1 migrations, ports and browser output. Normal success/discovery removes its snapshot; failures and explicit image capture retain private diagnostics in the printed temporary location.
+
+The snapshot's Vite app, fault Workers and `tests/support/db.ts` use the same canonical Wrangler configuration and persisted D1 directory. The shared async SQL helper uses Wrangler's SQL splitter, including trigger bodies, and independent SQL assertions. The live binding-identity regression verifies both directions. Worker-scoped fixtures dispose binding proxies; test-scoped fixtures provide distinct synthetic IPv4 clients so unrelated tests do not consume the same real sign-in limiter bucket. Limiter tests still prove denial and timed recovery without disabling the limiter.
+
+Schema faults, parked batches, one-time credentials and restart/recovery sequences remain ordered and use the production write path. `workers: 1` remains intentional within each snapshot; separate stores must be proven before adding in-suite parallelism. Fault Workers use runner-owned ports and the same snapshot store. No full-state reset occurs inside a causal scenario.
+
+Direct `pnpm exec playwright test` is available for discovery. Execute tests through `pnpm test:e2e`; the fixtures reject access to developer vars/DB outside an owned snapshot. `db:reset:local` is a separate, explicitly destructive developer database command; ordinary tests do not call it.
+
+## Presentation and private diagnostics
+
+`qualifyPresentation` always checks overflow, viewport/root-font transitions, draft preservation and reachable actions. Success PNGs are written only with `EFCC_CAPTURE_IMAGES=1`, including through `test:presentation`. Masking and source metadata remain attached to captured PNGs. Snapshot fingerprints identify executed working-tree inputs; staged runs also record the exact index tree and base HEAD. Capturing images does not establish physical-device/PWA/soft-keyboard behavior.
+
+Masked PNGs can be selected for review. The retained snapshot, raw traces, network recordings, logs and synthetic credential files remain private; screenshot masking does not sanitize those other artifacts.
+
+## Local gate and slim CI
+
+Pre-commit formats through lint-staged, then runs the staged gate once. Documentation-only changes avoid runtime startup. Fast test/type changes run check/typecheck/Vitest. Changed E2E files select those files; Home source selects its existing consumers. Shared auth/account/DB/fixture/configuration, unknown executable inputs and policy changes require the complete live inventory. Rename/deletion selection includes both names. Missing prerequisites, failed checks, unresolved conflicts, unclassified inputs or index drift cannot produce a success claim.
+
+The executing gate policy must be staged. The runner exports the index, installs pinned dependencies from the offline pnpm store without install hooks, and never auto-stages generated files. Unsupported symlink/submodule/LFS inputs fail clearly. A required tracked generated output must match the exported index; normal ignored Worker types are generated only inside the snapshot. Interruptions target owned process groups, not unrelated servers.
+
+GitHub Actions remains install + check/typecheck/Node Vitest. A local hook is bypassable; a local report is review evidence, not remote enforcement. Broad local qualification is required before handing off shared foundation changes. Run results qualify only their actual source tree, selected cases and projects.
+
+## Documentation references
+
+The design uses [Playwright fixtures](https://playwright.dev/docs/test-fixtures), [authentication isolation](https://playwright.dev/docs/auth), [projects](https://playwright.dev/docs/test-projects), [Wrangler binding proxies](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/wrangler/api/#getplatformproxy) and [Git index export](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-checkout-index). Context7 was used to verify the relevant current APIs; installed Wrangler 4.145.0 types and executed EFCC tests determine the actual runtime boundary.
